# OptiMax Pro-Tuner - Community Profile Database
#
# Fetched by the Community Profiles tab. DISPLAY ONLY: nothing here is ever
# applied automatically. A profile only takes effect after the user explicitly
# copies it into their own game library. Keep it that way - this file is
# remotely editable, so auto-applying anything in it would let whoever can edit
# it reconfigure every install.
#
# FORMAT - one game per line, six fields, pipe-separated, in this order:
#
#   exeName | disableSMT | highPriority | aggressiveRAMPurge | disableFSO | engineType
#
# Booleans: 1 / true / TRUE mean on. Anything else means off.
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# A line that does not have exactly six fields is skipped, as is any exeName
# that is not a plain filename ending in .exe. One bad line never invalidates
# the rest of the file.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE FLAGS ACTUALLY DO - read before editing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# disableSMT
#   Restricts the game to one thread per physical core. This HALVES the logical
#   processors available to it. It only helps a narrow set of latency-bound
#   titles on high core-count CPUs, and it costs real performance in anything
#   that scales with threads. Left off everywhere below by default - turn it on
#   only if you have measured a gain on your own hardware.
#
# highPriority
#   Raises the game to HIGH priority class. Helps when background work is
#   competing for CPU. Safe and modest.
#
# aggressiveRAMPurge
#   Trims working sets more often. Useful in long sessions on memory-tight
#   systems, but purging pages that get faulted straight back in can itself
#   cause hitching. Reserved below for titles with a known appetite for RAM.
#
# disableFSO
#   *** NOT PER-GAME, DESPITE LIVING IN A PER-GAME FILE. ***
#   It writes HKCU\System\GameConfigStore, which is a single per-user switch.
#   Setting it for one game disables Fullscreen Optimizations for EVERY game on
#   the system, and it stays disabled after that game exits (Settings >
#   Restore Windows Defaults reverses it). Because a user copying a profile for
#   one game would not expect a system-wide change, it is 0 on every line here.
#   Anyone who wants exclusive fullscreen should turn it on deliberately rather
#   than inherit it from a community profile.
#
# engineType
#   Display only. Free text, shown in the Community Profiles table.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTI-CHEAT NOTE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# disableSMT and highPriority are applied by opening a handle on the game
# process, so OptiMax deliberately SKIPS them whenever a kernel anti-cheat is
# running (Vanguard, EAC, BattlEye, FACEIT, GamersClub). Titles marked (AC)
# below will therefore ignore those two flags by design. This is intentional -
# a third-party handle on a protected process is not worth the risk.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Starter set. Extend it freely - exe names are matched exactly (case
# insensitive), so verify against Task Manager > Details before adding.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

